From 11dce655f90a0ed6bc8a0d17efdf37f3720813ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:05:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 49/88] h713: hdmi: RequestEDID reopens the gate only on a
 published EDID

RequestEDID closes the gate to read the DDC RAM and, as the blob does,
opens it again whenever the ready byte is set. After a ResetEDIDModule
without an upload that byte is set while publish() kept the gate closed
on the empty store (previous commit), so a G_EDID would have opened it
on whatever the RAM held. It now opens again only when the gate byte -
set by publish(), cleared by ResetEDIDModule - says an EDID is out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/hdmi/sun50i-h713-hdmi.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hdmi/sun50i-h713-hdmi.c b/drivers/hdmi/sun50i-h713-hdmi.c
index b85c475..87a81f5 100644
--- a/drivers/hdmi/sun50i-h713-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/hdmi/sun50i-h713-hdmi.c
@@ -555,7 +555,9 @@ group_15(uint8_t hi)
 		 * read and opens again after the four frames (0x11cac(7, 0) and
 		 * (7, 1), the latter only with the EDID ready). With the gate
 		 * open the RAM belongs to the DDC side and reads as zero, from
-		 * the AR100 and from the ARM alike (HY310, 07.10.2026).
+		 * the AR100 and from the ARM alike (HY310, 07.10.2026). It
+		 * opens again only on an EDID publish() put out (the gate
+		 * byte), not on the empty store after a ResetEDIDModule.
 		 */
 		aux_gate(0x7, false);
 		for (uint8_t idx = 0; idx < 4; ++idx) {
@@ -565,7 +567,7 @@ group_15(uint8_t hi)
 			frame[69] = 0;
 			reply_frame(frame, 72);
 		}
-		if (sh_rd8(SH_EDID_READY))
+		if (sh_rd8(SH_EDID_READY) && sh_rd8(SH_EDID_GATE))
 			aux_gate(0x7, true);
 	}
 }
